ALBUKHR Contributor Internal Dashboard V1

FILES
- contributor-internal-dashboard.html
- js/contributor/internal-dashboard.js
- css/contributor-internal-dashboard.css

DEPLOY ORDER
1. Deploy the API patch:
   albukhr-api-internal-liquidity-v1.zip

2. In albukhr-app, place:
   - contributor-internal-dashboard.html at repository root
   - js/contributor/internal-dashboard.js under js/contributor/
   - css/contributor-internal-dashboard.css under css/

3. Open:
   https://app.albukhr.com/contributor-internal-dashboard.html

CURRENT SCOPE
- Mainnet-only.
- Uses existing Pi Auth Core, Page Auth Guard and ALBUKHR API Core.
- Contributor ownership is checked by the server.
- Add Liquidity uses:
  /api/internal-liquidity-approve
  /api/internal-liquidity-complete
- Treasury/readiness uses:
  /api/internal-liquidity-workspace
- History uses:
  /api/internal-liquidity-history
- No LocalStorage/sessionStorage.
- No direct browser financial table access.
- No changes to Core staking or Core financial gateway.
- No Dock Navigation changes.

IMPORTANT CURRENT STATE
Maitagogo is approved, but its Mainnet Internal treasury is currently not configured.
The dashboard will intentionally show Add Liquidity as locked until the treasury is configured.
Do not manually activate the project or mark the Internal runtime ready.
